      "problem": "Matt and Abraham have the same number of marbles. A total of $63%$ of Matt's marbles are blue, while $\\frac{3}{4}$ of Abraham's marbles are blue. Select the options that make the statements below true.\n\n$\\,$\nA total of \n{{field-1}}\nof Abraham's marbles are blue. \n\n$\\,$\nTherefore, he has \n{{field-2}}\nblue marbles compared to Matt.",
      "worked_solution": "We need to compare $\\frac{3}{4}$ with $63%.$ We can do this by writing $\\frac{3}{4}$ as a percent.\n\nFirst, we write $\\frac{3}{4}$ as an equivalent fraction with $100$ as the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{4}=\\frac{3\\times 25}{4\\times 25}=\\frac{75}{100}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write this fraction as a percentage:\n\n$$\n\\frac{75}{100}=75%\n$$\n\nSince $75%>63%,$ we have the following:\n\n- A total of $75%$ of Abraham's marbles are blue.\n\n- Therefore, he has $\\text{more}$ blue marbles compared to Matt.",
